      "hints": [
        "Equate $f'(a) = -\\frac{3}{(a + 2)^4} = -\\frac{16}{27}$.",
        "Cross-multiply to get $16(a + 2)^4 = 81 \\implies (a + 2)^2 = \\frac{9}{4}$.",
        "Take square roots $a + 2 = \\pm\\frac{3}{2}$ and solve for both values of $a$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Equate the derivative at $x = a$ to the given gradient of the tangent:\n$$-\\frac{3}{(a + 2)^4} = -\\frac{16}{27} \\implies \\frac{3}{(a + 2)^4} = \\frac{16}{27}$$",
        "Cross-multiply and isolate $(a + 2)^4$:\n$$16(a + 2)^4 = 81 \\implies (a + 2)^4 = \\frac{81}{16}$$",
        "Take the square root of both sides:\n$$(a + 2)^2 = \\frac{9}{4} \\implies a + 2 = \\pm\\frac{3}{2}$$",
        "Solve for both possible values of $a$:\n$$a = \\frac{3}{2} - 2 = -\\frac{1}{2}$$\n$$a = -\\frac{3}{2} - 2 = -\\frac{7}{2}$$"
      ],
